.SS stopInit
.EX
i32 stopInit();
.EE
.PP
Make SIGINT and SIGTERM request a clean stop instead of ending the program: each sets signal.stopRequested and makes the returned fd readable, for a poll() loop to notice. The handlers use SA_RESTART and SA_RESETHAND, so a second SIGINT or SIGTERM ends the program as usual (a way out if the loop never stops). The fd is non-blocking and close-on-exec; reading it is optional. Returns the same fd on later calls, -1 if the pipe can't be made. Call it once, before starting threads.
